* Afternoon watch (14:55)  Mr Travers: on passage (bound for Funchal via Ushant, Finisterre); his book 'on passage' loaded: the leg, trim to the course, trim on a shift, tend the sheets, bearings, pilot water, the lead in pilot water, the anchorage, shorten sail for weather, the pilot boards, the pilot aboard, the pilot put off, the pilot off, under way again.
* Afternoon watch (14:55)  By the captain, on passage: shaping a course for funchal road.
  Afternoon watch (14:55)  Shaped a course for Funchal Road: SW by account, 10 miles; the line crosses the land about Machico. Helm ordered: steer SW (221°).
! Afternoon watch (14:55)  She has taken the ground forward: one fathom and a half of water by the chart, and she draws 11 feet; she struck at half a knot, heeling 0 degrees, the tide rising.
